      "title": "Intel’s EMIB-T takes aim at TSMC’s CoWoS-L as AI chip packaging gets crowded - Crypto Briefing",
      "date": "2026-11-05",
      "source": "Crypto Briefing",
      "url": "https://cryptobriefing.com/intel-emib-t-vs-tsmc-cowos-l/",
      "summary": "Intel’s EMIB-T takes aim at TSMC’s CoWoS-L as AI chip packaging gets crowded Crypto Briefing",
      "body": "Intel is pitching its bridge-based packaging as a higher-yield, lower-cost alternative while TSMC's CoWoS capacity stays fully booked\nIntel wants a bigger piece of the AI chip boom, and it is not starting with the chips themselves. It is starting with the packaging that holds them together.\nThe company expects future AI packages to carry more than 32 HBM stacks and over 70 EMIB bridges. That is a lot of hardware crammed into one slab, and Intel is betting its EMIB-T technology can handle it more efficiently than TSMC’s CoWoS-L.\nWhat Intel is actually selling\nTSMC’s CoWoS approach has historically leaned on a large silicon interposer, essentially a big slab of silicon that everything sits on. CoWoS-L, the version in question, is the variant now drawing direct comparisons with Intel’s offering.\nIntel’s EMIB-T takes a different route. Instead of one giant silicon foundation, it embeds small, localized silicon bridges inside an organic substrate, placing silicon only where chips need to ta",
